title: Managed Codex app-server delivery + gated auto-turn (shipped B131)
---
SHIPPED in B131 (2026-07-12). On supported Codex versions, `c2c start codex` / `c2c new codex` use an authenticated loopback app-server transport by default, with automatic fallback to hooks when unavailable.

Managed supervision injects inbound c2c mail into model-visible history on arrival and starts one gated turn for eligible local-broker mail when the thread is explicitly idle and DND is off. Active or unknown-status arrivals remain queued and batch into one follow-up turn after completion; turns are intentionally never steered or interrupted. Relay/remote mail is inject-only and cannot start a turn, preserving the B098 bus-not-RPC invariant.

Thread/session lifecycle, restart/resume, truthful delivery-mode diagnostics, and operator documentation are shipped. Vanilla Codex retains `poll-inbox` / `wait-inbox` as the portable fallback. Any future automatic response-forwarding enhancement should be tracked separately rather than reopening this worker-mode idea.
